<title>USA: Greyhound Oct passenger sales up.</title>
<headline>Greyhound Oct passenger sales up.</headline>
<dateline>DALLAS 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greyhound Lines Inc.</p>
<p>			   October Traffic Statistics (1)</p>
<p>			   (in 000's except where noted)</p>
<p>198 Locations	     October 1996    October 1995    Change</p>
<p>Passengers (2)		    998		 948	   5.3%</p>
<p>Passenger Sales (2)	 $32,039	   $29,995	   6.8%</p>
<p>Passenger Miles (2)	 354,271	   334,536	   5.9%</p>
<p>Yield (Sales per Passenger</p>
<p>Mile) (cents) (2)</p>
<p>				     9.04		8.97	   0.8%</p>
<p>Average Trip Length (miles) (2)</p>
<p>					355		 353	   0.6%</p>
<p>System-wide</p>
<p>Regular Service Miles (3)  20,575	    19,786	   4.0%</p>
<p>Available Seat Miles (3)  946,450	   910,156	   4.0%</p>
<p>1) Statistics do not include the company's bus operating subsidiaries. Traffic information may differ from information previously reported due to continued refinements in the company's data analysis systems.  </p>
<p>2) Statistics are for sales generated by 198 of the company's largest locations which electronically report sales. Same locations are used for 1995 and 1996 and represent about 72 percent of total monthly sales. The company's smaller locations have not shown the same rate of growth in sales and passenger counts. Sales totals must be adjusted for refunds, unredeemed tickets, interline activity and other miscellaneous items to reflect revenues and related statistics for financial statement purposes.</p>
<p>3) Includes all Greyhound Lines Inc locations. Does not include bus operating subsidiaries.</p>
</text>
